# Listings Project

Personal Streamlit app for searching NYC listings on listingsproject.com. **App-only** — no CLI/bash scripts.

## Files

- `app.py` — Streamlit UI: filters, card grid, CSV export
- `listing_scraper.py` — fetches and parses the live NYC index HTML

Run: `streamlit run app.py`

## Architecture

1. `fetch_all_listings()` crawls all index pages once
2. `@st.cache_data` in `app.py` caches the full crawl; **Refresh listings** clears cache
3. Borough, neighborhood, and date filters run **in memory** on cached rows — no re-crawl on filter change

## Data model (`ListingRow`)

Parsed from each index card on `https://www.listingsproject.com/real-estate/new-york-city`:

| Field | Source |
|-------|--------|
| `neighborhood_name` | Text before borough in location line (raw, as published) |
| `neighborhood_names` | Canonical name(s) from alias map + fuzzy match; multi-hood listings map to all matches |
| `borough_label` / `borough_key` | Derived from location line |
| `listing_type` | Segment after first `\|` (e.g. "Apartments for Sublet") |
| `description` | `<p class="text-sm leading-normal mb-4">` on card |
| `listing_start` / `listing_end` | Availability dates on card |
| `photo_url`, `title`, `price`, `url` | Standard card fields |

Location line format: `Neighborhood, Borough | Type | optional tags`

## Borough rules

- Brooklyn/Queens/Bronx/Staten Island: match borough name in location line
- **Manhattan**: `, New York` with no other borough token (best-effort heuristic)
- Neighborhood dropdown and cards use **canonical** names (`neighborhood_names`), not raw strings. Aliases live in `NEIGHBORHOOD_ALIASES` in `listing_scraper.py` (e.g. "Bed Stuy" / "Bed-Stuy" → "Bedford-Stuyvesant"). Unmatched/junk tokens are dropped. Multi-neighborhood listings (e.g. "Bed-Stuy/Clinton Hill") appear under every matched hood. Cards show joined canonical names (raw kept for CSV).

## Date filters (app.py)

- **Any dates** (default): no date filter
- **Dates** (check-in / check-out): listing must cover the full window — `listing_start <= check_in` and `listing_end >= check_out`; tolerance expands the required window via `_expand_date_range`
- **Flexible**: stay length gates the match against any selected month. **Month** → listing must cover the entire month (`listing_start <= month_start` and `listing_end >= month_end`); **Week** → listing must offer a continuous `WEEK_STAY_DAYS` window inside the month. See `_listing_covers_month_stay` / `_listing_covers_week_stay`.

## Parser maintenance

HTML selectors in `listing_scraper.py` drift when the site changes. Key regexes: `CARD_SPLIT_RE`, `HOOD_RE`, `TITLE_LINK_RE`. Card wrapper is `flex flex-col md:flex-row`; location line uses `text-grey-dark  text-smish`.

## Scope

- Extend filters and results UX in `app.py`; keep parsing logic in `listing_scraper.py`
- Detail pages are fetched **on demand only** for photo galleries (`fetch_listing_photo_urls` / first carousel › click) — do not crawl detail pages during the index refresh
- Minimize scope; match existing code style
